00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:00.650
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:02.050
Wa! Shoi!

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:05.720
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:10.730
Even an absurd response

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:13.630
Is sensible for someone from Jupiter

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:15.730
Launch a rocket at random

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:18.570
And approach the place where it lands

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:23.230
After a pleasant nap

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:27.650
Sure enough, sure enough,
my eyes tear when I yawn

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:28.810
Good morning

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:29.980
Let's play!

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.680
Let's have a serious bread-eating race

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:33.820
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.350
Who, who, who, who, who is it?

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:39.690
Hungry, hungry, hungry,
hungry, hungry person

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:44.100
Girls live off snacks

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:45.860
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!
Rolling, rolling, rolling, golfing around

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:46.660
Rolling, rolling, rolling, golfing around

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:50.000
Lazing, lazing, lazing, lazing, lazing about

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.910
Let's look up at the sun

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:57.180
Wasshoi! Wasshoi!

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:59.710
In a dream, in a dream with everyone
Wasshoi! Wasshoi!

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:02.280
I had the same conversation

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:06.180
Question mark and washoi 365

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:07.980
Wasshoi! Washoshoi!

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:13.780
Hohokekyo!
My Neighbors XXXXXX-XXn
March 25, Congrats Chika

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:21.160
All we have to do is wait for our guest.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:22.650
I wonder if she'll be coming soon?

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:26.730
Sorry, you didn't have to do all this.

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:28.600
I did things too.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:31.800
It's the least we could do for your little sister.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.370
I'm being ignored!

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:34.840
It's not that big a deal.

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:37.380
Miya-chan, what is this supposed to be?

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.480
A goldfish?

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:39.480
Sea bream.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:41.450
Or so it's supposed to be.
Doesn't it look like one?

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:45.840
Coming!

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:47.640
I'm coming in!

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:49.840
Sis, this is from Mom.

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:53.650
I'm worn out. I rushed here from the station.

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:55.220
Thanks.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:56.720
What is this?

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:57.900
It's all sorts of things.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:01.460
Pumpkin, ham, instant foods and snacks.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.790
Hello! Long time no see.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:05.800
Oh, Hiro, hello!

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:07.960
Nice to see you again.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:09.670
Here're some cookies.

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:12.300
You didn't have to get anything for me.

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:14.100
Come on in.

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:15.610
Okay!

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:17.820
Yuno! Miyako!

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:19.280
Long time no see!

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:20.790
Congratulations on your acceptance!

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:21.980
Congrats!

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.980
Oh, this is the CD I was talking about.

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:29.920
It's not very good, so just skip through it.

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.060
Thank you, I'm looking forward to it!

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:34.400
I see you grew a little, Chika.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.430
Really?

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:36.990
If I did, that's great!

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:38.640
You did too!

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.300
Really? I guess it's because I sleep a lot.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:43.270
You're so talkative.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.480
Chika, would you like some tea?

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:47.770
If you're hungry, let's have dinner.

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:49.570
Umm, either is fine.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:51.740
Amazing!

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.870
Are these homemade?

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:57.510
Yeah, I heard you like gyoza.

00:03:57.820 --> 00:03:59.920
Everyone helped to make them.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:02.580
Thank you, I'm really happy!

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:06.390
What's this supposed to be? Candy?

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:08.560
I guess it doesn't look like a sea bream, huh?

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:10.300
It was a sea bream?!

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:16.670
It's hot, but it's delicious!

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:19.170
It's incredibly delicious!

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:22.870
I'm jealous you get to live next to Hiro.

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:24.850
Thank you.

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:27.510
But I don't make elaborate things every day.

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:31.790
I just usually make small side dishes
or things that I can make quickly.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:34.460
You can make anything, can't you, Hiro?

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:37.920
Do you cook anything, Sis?

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:42.460
How rude! I cook things.

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:43.670
For example?

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:46.800
Spaghetti, curry and ramen...

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:48.000
Instant foods?

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:49.670
It doesn't matter what they are.

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:52.540
Now, now, Sae is busy with work.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:54.640
Mom is worried.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.850
She wants you to call once in a while.

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:59.540
Yeah, I know.

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:06.280
This is bliss!

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:09.460
How odd.

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:14.630
This is only the second time I've come to the
Hidamari Apartments, but I feel so at home.

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:15.600
I wonder why?

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.990
Hurray for Hidamari Apartments!

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:20.130
What was that for, Miyako?

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:23.670
This truly is a strange place.

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:27.040
It's right in front of the school,
and yet, it's oddly peaceful.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:29.710
If we hear the warning bell, we'll make
it to school in time if we run!

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:32.210
No, we don't even have to run.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:36.620
If we don't run when the warning
bell rings, we'll be late.

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:40.690
I'm no good with mornings, so I might have
a hard time living anywhere else.

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:43.560
During lunch breaks we can
go home and take naps.

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:44.930
What? Really?

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:48.100
I'd like to do do that before I graduate!

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.720
Is that all? You had me there for a second!

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:54.930
I get most tired during the first
class in the afternoon.

00:05:55.070 --> 00:05:58.240
It's right after you fill your stomach
with food after all.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:03.080
Come to think of it, Miya-chan, you often
sleep during your afternoon classes.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:05.410
You sleep pretty often too, Yunocchi.

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:08.080
Y-You think so?

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:11.890
High-school life sure is wonderful!

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:15.790
Chika, you mustn't copy these girls!

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:20.620
Yuno aside, Miyako does whatever
she feels like doing.

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:23.500
You do the same thing, Sis!

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:25.390
What do you mean?

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:28.070
You do whatever you like.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:31.070
You write novels and live on your own.

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:33.110
You decided it all on your own.

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:34.440
Well...

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:37.600
There's nothing wrong with
deciding my own life.

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:39.110
That's true...

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:41.470
But you keep going further ahead of me.

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:43.910
I'm going to a normal high school.

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:46.520
I played brass instruments in middle school,

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:49.580
but I don't think I'm going to be
doing that in the future.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:53.290
Umm...

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:58.170
I think everyone has their own strong points.

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:00.400
Yes, I think so too.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:01.240
Huh?

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:06.370
I think you have some wonderful way of
spending your time that only you can do.

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:09.410
Huh? You think so?

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:11.820
She's just like her.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:13.580
They really are sisters.

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:17.920
You two! Mind your own business!

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:21.560
What are you going to do after this?

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:23.830
Is there anywhere you want to go with Chika?

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:26.320
Huh? Aren't we going to karaoke?

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:27.500
Karaoke?

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:32.740
Yeah, Chika and I talked about
going to karaoke.

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:33.470
Yeah!

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:33.940
Is that so? You should have said so earlier.
Yeah!

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:37.070
Is that so? You should have said so earlier.

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:38.600
Karaoke, huh?

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:41.870
It all seems so long ago.

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:43.650
What are you talking about?

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:45.150
We just went...

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:46.880
But I guess...

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:49.590
Yeah, we haven't gone in a while, have we?

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:51.490
Then, why don't we all go?

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:52.820
All right!

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:54.550
I want to go!

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:56.360
What?!

00:07:56.360 --> 00:07:56.990
Closing Temporarily
We will not be doing business until
the 31st due to renovations.
Owner

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:57.600
Closing Temporarily
We will not be doing business until
the 31st due to renovations.
Owner
It says they're not doing business
until the 31st due to renovations.

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:01.660
It says they're not doing business
until the 31st due to renovations.

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:03.100
We've been foiled.

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:05.040
Sorry, Chika.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:07.300
There's no need for you to apologize, Yuno.

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:09.270
Chika, it can't be helped.

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:10.440
Yeah...

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:13.680
You were really looking forward to it.
I'm really sorry.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:16.010
It's really all right.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:18.210
Things like this happen.

00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:22.580
Huh? It's the landlady.

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:25.050
Oh, you're right.

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:26.290
Hey!

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:29.380
Hello! Is that your new part-time job?

00:08:29.590 --> 00:08:31.360
I have a day off today.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:33.400
I'm going to go night fishing.

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:36.430
Well, don't expect me to get you any
souvenirs or to split anything with you.

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:39.870
If you hadn't said anything,
I wouldn't have expected anything.

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:41.130
Who's she?

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:43.070
She's Hidamari Apartments' landlady.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:44.770
Oh?

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:49.000
Oh yeah, I'm going to pick up that
thing from Room 203 soon.

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:51.750
Okay, come any time.

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:55.450
I mean, please come as soon as possible.

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:00.220
Later!

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:03.690
That thing from Room 203?

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:04.190
Yamabuki

00:09:07.630 --> 00:09:10.230
Hello, Principal.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:13.960
Hello. How is spring break?

00:09:14.310 --> 00:09:16.670
It's been very lively.

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:21.200
I'm doing my best too. Energetic is best.

00:09:21.650 --> 00:09:23.270
Well, see you all later.

00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:25.140
See you later.

00:09:26.650 --> 00:09:27.780
He's fast!

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:31.480
Look out! Move out of the way!

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:34.120
Ms. Yoshinoya?
Yosshi?

00:09:34.290 --> 00:09:36.890
Oh, I see you're all together.

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:38.790
Long time no see, Chika.

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:41.430
You remembered me!

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:43.400
Long time no see, Ms. Yoshinoya!

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:45.930
What are you doing?

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:50.310
Well, the principal is angry with me.

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:53.040
I have too many personal belongings,

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:56.050
so he wants me to get rid of all
of them during spring break.

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:57.280
Isn't that cruel?

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:59.280
It serves you right.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:01.320
Those are some strange personal belongings.

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:05.760
Were you thinking of helping
me a little just now?

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:08.660
Come on! Please!

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:09.790
Umm...

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:12.790
What can I do to help?

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:25.710
Umm, is there anything I can do to help?

00:10:25.860 --> 00:10:28.220
Chika, you're our guest today.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:29.250
Northern Sea Marine Products

00:10:29.490 --> 00:10:32.130
Thank you for waiting! It's thawing nicely!

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:33.100
What is that?

00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:33.430
Northern Sea Marine Products
What is that?

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:34.420
Northern Sea Marine Products

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:38.130
The things that take longer to cook go in first.

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:39.330
Let's begin.

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:42.470
The bounty and final hope
of the northern seas!

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:43.610
Crab!

00:10:43.610 --> 00:10:44.970
Amazing!

00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:47.140
Miya-chan, I'm surprised you saved that.

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:51.710
I was close to eating it many times,
but I held back for this day!

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:53.770
Huh? For me?

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:57.440
Yeah, anyway, it's more fun
to eat it with everyone.

00:10:57.750 --> 00:11:03.250
Yeah! I'm so jealous. I want to move here!

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:04.590
Out of the question!

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:06.330
That's not fair, Sis!

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:08.730
You get to have so much fun every day!

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:11.560
We don't always eat together.

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:14.000
Miya-chan, you can put in the crab already.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:16.330
Here I go.

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:18.970
Wow!

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:22.650
D-Delicious!

00:11:22.650 --> 00:11:24.200
It's nice and hot!

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:26.480
It's difficult to eat hot foods.

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:28.920
Hot pots really warm you up, don't they?

00:11:29.050 --> 00:11:30.420
Yeah...

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:33.760
Here, Chika, this leg looks easy to eat.

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:36.120
Thank you very much!

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:39.560
This sweetness truly is the bounty
of the northern seas!

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:45.470
It was my first time at a public bath!

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:48.270
The conversation has finally started again.

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:48.740
Mt. Fuji

00:11:49.010 --> 00:11:54.140
A Ione northern sea gull...

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:57.410
Swaying at the mercy of the waves...

00:11:57.410 --> 00:12:01.880
Wandering to a port town...

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:11.160
The moon is covered in haze tonight...

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:12.730
Enka?!

00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:14.630
And she's really good!

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:16.170
Didn't I tell you?

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:18.100
Miya-chan is a pro!

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:19.470
Huh? No way!

00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:21.460
She might make a professional debut.

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:23.040
No, I won't!

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:24.740
Come on, Yunocchi, you're next!

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:26.370
Huh? Huh? Me?

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:33.920
Outside of the window...

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:39.120
I look up towards the blue sky...

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:42.530
I'm enjoying the moment...

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:44.190
Dream Glider!

00:12:44.190 --> 00:12:44.430
This is Dream Glider, isn't it?
It sounds kind of different.

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:46.760
A voice that calls the wind...
This is Dream Glider, isn't it?
It sounds kind of different.

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:48.760
Gazing at the distant clouds...
This is Dream Glider, isn't it?
It sounds kind of different.

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:49.700
I fly across the sky...
This is Dream Glider, isn't it?
It sounds kind of different.

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:50.730
I fly across the sky...

00:12:50.730 --> 00:12:53.100
I fly across the sky...
Don't mind the details.

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:55.100
That's wonderful, Yuno!

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:57.570
Come on, let's all sing now.

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:04.350
The seasons change and
winter turns to spring...

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:07.880
Just like the constellations
in the sky change...

00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:12.680
My seasons change as well...

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:19.160
I never expected that in
return for helping you.

00:13:19.300 --> 00:13:21.630
Miya-chan, were you expecting more?

00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:23.120
Kind of...

00:13:23.270 --> 00:13:25.700
That was really fun, wasn't it?

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:29.510
We got to take a bath with
Ms. Yoshinoya and sing with her.

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:31.130
That doesn't happen too often.

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:35.110
It's really been a while since
I took a bath with you, Sis!

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:38.150
What is it?

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:40.170
It's nothing.

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:43.850
You were thinking about how
I got bigger, weren't you?

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:47.320
No, I was thinking about how you haven't
changed since you were little.

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:51.450
Is that so?! Well, you haven't changed
since middle school.

00:13:51.690 --> 00:13:54.490
The conversation is so
awkward I can't join in.

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:58.120
Perhaps we should tell them
the objective truth.

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:00.800
What's this? Are you sharing secrets?

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:03.070
Let me join in!

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:05.000
It's nothing.

00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:07.910
We were just talking about
how unfortunate it was

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:10.740
that we couldn't go to karaoke
because the store was closed.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.540
Is that so?

00:14:12.880 --> 00:14:15.650
Well, if you want to sing, you can do it here.

00:14:16.590 --> 00:14:18.620
There's a nice echo here too.

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:20.290
Let's sing together.

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:21.220
B-But...

00:14:21.220 --> 00:14:23.260
Come on, don't hold back.

00:14:23.260 --> 00:14:24.860
Lalala!

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:28.300
The beginning of love is always...

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:29.600
Yeah!

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:31.370
Lululu...

00:14:31.370 --> 00:14:35.300
Quite a happening!

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:38.910
Is Ms. Yoshinoya like that all the time?

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:41.580
If anything, she was always like that.

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:45.600
I'd like a fun teacher like
her at my high school.

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:47.650
You can take her with you.

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:49.410
I'm sure you'll have mixed feelings.

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.710
Can I take this?

00:14:56.090 --> 00:14:58.430
Even if I lie...

00:14:58.430 --> 00:14:59.360
What does it matter?!

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:01.560
Even if people get angry with me...

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:02.600
What does it matter?!

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:08.870
Today I feel like doing bad
things I shouldn't do...

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:12.010
What does it matter?! What does it matter?!

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:15.680
So, forgive me for today...

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:17.550
I wonder if people can hear us from outside?

00:15:17.550 --> 00:15:19.540
Let's stop if someone comes in.

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:23.190
I thought about it afterwards,

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:26.790
but I'm surprised no one said anything
to us about our singing.

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:29.550
To be honest, my heart was racing.

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:34.460
I'm sure they're just used to
Yamabuki High School's weirdos.

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:36.400
So that's it!

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:38.260
Don't agree with that!

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:40.640
I'm satisfied.

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:42.540
Miya-chan, when did you finish it off?!

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:46.470
I thought that we shouldn't waste
one drop of that crab soup.

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:48.680
Well done.

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:50.510
I'm going to clean up.

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:52.270
We've got more.

00:15:52.580 --> 00:15:53.840
Wow!

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:56.120
Here I go!

00:15:57.150 --> 00:15:57.880
Congratulations On Your Acceptance

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:01.620
Congratulations, Chika!

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:03.430
Is this for me?!

00:16:03.430 --> 00:16:05.830
Of course, this is a celebration after all.

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:08.330
Here's a present from everyone!

00:16:08.430 --> 00:16:09.520
What?

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:13.530
Can I open it?

00:16:13.670 --> 00:16:14.760
Yeah!

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:19.160
You said that you liked this shop.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:21.510
Wow, what should I do?

00:16:21.510 --> 00:16:23.250
You've done so much for me.

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:25.340
Thank you, everyone!

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:27.620
Don't be so stiff!

00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:28.880
Here you go.

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:31.920
Bon appétit!

00:16:32.350 --> 00:16:34.080
Aren't you glad, Chika?

00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:35.650
Yeah!

00:16:36.960 --> 00:16:39.550
What a wonderful day!

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:41.300
Today is special.

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:44.330
Try not to ruin your daily schedule
over spring break.

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:46.890
Sae, no lectures today!

00:16:47.740 --> 00:16:49.140
Okay...

00:16:49.740 --> 00:16:51.970
You sister is just not good at
expressing her feelings.

00:16:53.810 --> 00:16:55.370
I'm well aware of that.

00:16:55.680 --> 00:16:58.170
Sisters sure are wonderful.

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:03.210
I'm stuffed. I'm feeling tired.

00:17:03.450 --> 00:17:06.320
I have snacks, but I can't eat anymore.

00:17:06.320 --> 00:17:07.850
Huh? What kind of snacks?

00:17:08.560 --> 00:17:10.820
Chocolates, rice crackers and the usual.

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:12.620
I don't have anything unusual.

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:15.330
I want to eat something strange
once in a while.

00:17:15.330 --> 00:17:18.200
By strange snacks,
do you mean like that thing?

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:19.100
What do you mean?

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:22.100
You know, that thing that doesn't
even have a name.

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:23.670
Haven't you seen the commercials?

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:25.540
I remember!

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:27.810
I thought they stopped making those.

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:29.210
They still sell it.

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:30.750
What?!

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:32.180
They still sell it?!

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:33.850
I didn't know that!

00:17:33.850 --> 00:17:36.040
That really was a snack?

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:37.880
How did it taste?

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:40.490
It didn't taste good.

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:41.790
It doesn't taste good?

00:17:42.630 --> 00:17:43.360
Yeah...

00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:43.760
How disappointing...
Yeah...

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:44.850
How disappointing...

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:48.330
Chika, are you going to join
any clubs in high school?

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:50.170
You were in the brass band, weren't you?

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:52.640
Yeah, but it was really tough.

00:17:52.640 --> 00:17:54.540
I was wondering what I should do.

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:57.370
Did you think of joining a sports team?

00:17:57.370 --> 00:17:59.860
Yes, I like moving my body.

00:18:00.110 --> 00:18:03.080
That will make you the opposite of your sister.

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:05.980
It's not that I hate moving my body.

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:07.980
I just like writing more.

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:09.990
I'm a pretty fast runner.

00:18:09.990 --> 00:18:11.610
You're also good at tennis.

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:16.530
It's no exaggeration when I say that Sae's
pretty much a boy at Yamabuki High School.

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:19.960
You said that before, but it's an exaggeration!

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:23.370
Come to think of it,
she plays the male parts in plays.

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:25.370
Yeah, I know.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.340
It was the same in middle school.

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:30.110
She's tall, and she is the way she is.

00:18:30.110 --> 00:18:33.710
Because of that, she used to receive Valentine's
Day chocolates from girls in her class.

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:35.040
I knew it!

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:37.150
What do you mean by that?!

00:18:37.150 --> 00:18:40.950
Is that a part of your abundant
experience in love?

00:18:40.950 --> 00:18:44.610
No! Chika, this isn't important!

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:46.890
There's no need to hide it.

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:50.420
Even as a girl, I think you're cool.

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:52.900
What a bold statement.

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:55.430
She didn't mean it like that.

00:18:55.430 --> 00:18:58.960
Right? Sae really is cool.

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:04.200
U-Umm, did I say something strange?

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:06.710
No, you're spot on, Yunocchi.

00:19:06.710 --> 00:19:07.740
Huh? Huh?

00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:11.010
Thank you for praising my sister, Yuno!

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:14.310
Umm, you're welcome.

00:19:14.980 --> 00:19:17.550
Now, what should we do tomorrow?

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:18.650
What should we do?

00:19:18.790 --> 00:19:21.720
If the weather's good,
it might be nice to go out.

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:23.330
Yeah, that sounds good.

00:19:23.330 --> 00:19:25.930
I don't have anything to do
today or tomorrow.

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:28.730
Let's wrap things up for today.

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:31.570
Chika, you're staying at Sae's place, right?

00:19:31.930 --> 00:19:34.700
Yes, just as long as we don't fight again.

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:36.710
It will be all right.

00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:40.140
You're welcome to visit me late at night.

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:43.210
Okay! Well, goodnight.

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:47.180
Goodnight!

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:53.150
That was fun! A day full of
excitement just went right by!

00:19:54.160 --> 00:19:55.750
It sure went by quickly.

00:19:56.330 --> 00:19:58.850
It would be great if every day was like this!

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:00.830
Every day?

00:20:00.830 --> 00:20:05.060
We live pretty thrifty and
boring lives, you know.

00:20:05.630 --> 00:20:09.000
Settle down a little when you
become a high school student.

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:12.340
You don't have to tell me that!

00:20:14.010 --> 00:20:16.170
But I am kind of jealous.

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:17.780
Of what?

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:19.310
Living on your own.

00:20:19.310 --> 00:20:23.320
You have friends the same age as you whom
you can rely on and have fun with.

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:26.120
It's difficult to make friends
who are the same age as you

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:28.190
if you don't stay at a place
like this or a dorm.

00:20:28.190 --> 00:20:32.460
Besides, if you left home,
Mom and Dad would be sad.

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:38.800
That's true, but that's not fair,
since you left home before me.

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:42.030
Say, Sis...

00:20:43.070 --> 00:20:44.140
What?

00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:47.610
Did you pick out that handkerchief
with Yuno and the others?

00:20:47.610 --> 00:20:51.050
No, Hiro and the others bought that.

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:04.550
Sis?

00:21:04.830 --> 00:21:05.950
Open it up.

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:07.250
Okay!

00:21:11.600 --> 00:21:13.030
Wow!

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:15.000
It's beautiful!

00:21:15.240 --> 00:21:16.910
You're going to high school,

00:21:16.910 --> 00:21:19.530
so I thought it might be nice if you
had something more mature.

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:21.940
Is this for me?

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:22.810
Yes...

00:21:22.810 --> 00:21:25.610
Thank you! I'm really happy!

00:21:28.980 --> 00:21:30.350
It is a celebration after all.

00:21:30.820 --> 00:21:31.950
Yeah!

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:33.420
Maezawa Private Middle School
Brass Band
Concert Gold Medal

00:21:33.820 --> 00:21:36.620
What's this? Concert gold medal?

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:38.450
Play
Pause

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:45.830
Wow! She's really good!

00:21:48.970 --> 00:21:51.630
I already took a bath today.

00:21:52.210 --> 00:21:53.570
Oh well...

00:21:53.740 --> 00:21:55.440
It would be a waste if I didn't.

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:58.370
I wonder if Chika is still awake?

00:21:58.910 --> 00:22:00.850
I wonder if they're sleeping in the same bed?

00:22:04.850 --> 00:22:06.980
I'm sure that today will be all right.

00:22:07.520 --> 00:22:09.990
March 25 The End
To Be Continued
Answer: Dinner

00:22:19.430 --> 00:22:25.740
An unknown world stretched out

00:22:25.740 --> 00:22:31.480
Connecting, endless connecting threads

00:22:32.110 --> 00:22:38.520
An upside down world is pretty fun

00:22:38.520 --> 00:22:44.320
Connecting, never-ending threads

00:22:44.690 --> 00:22:50.390
You are smiling somewhere today

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:55.970
I will run all night until the day we meet again

00:22:55.970 --> 00:22:57.570
Run all night

00:22:57.570 --> 00:23:00.640
The record of a resounding shooting star

00:23:00.640 --> 00:23:03.980
Your singing voice

00:23:03.980 --> 00:23:07.050
Touches my heart

00:23:07.050 --> 00:23:10.320
A sky full of shooting stars

00:23:10.320 --> 00:23:13.460
The record of a shining shooting star

00:23:13.460 --> 00:23:16.660
Your whispering voice

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:20.100
Leads me through space

00:23:20.100 --> 00:23:22.970
A song about shooting stars

00:23:22.970 --> 00:23:26.500
I can't hear them

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:30.440
I can't reach them

00:23:30.440 --> 00:23:35.000
The footsteps I'm looking for

00:23:40.070 --> 00:23:41.230
Preview

00:23:41.230 --> 00:23:43.400
Preview
Say, could you help me with some research?

00:23:43.400 --> 00:23:44.970
Preview
Do you think aliens exist?

00:23:44.970 --> 00:23:46.910
Preview
Do you think the red string really exists?

00:23:46.910 --> 00:23:49.480
Preview
I think aliens and the red string are pranks.

00:23:49.480 --> 00:23:51.080
Preview
No, they're not.

00:23:51.080 --> 00:23:53.210
Preview
I'm not sure.

00:23:53.210 --> 00:23:57.050
Preview
I believe in the red string.
I wonder who I'm connected to?

00:23:57.050 --> 00:23:58.180
Preview
The principal.

00:23:58.180 --> 00:23:59.890
Preview
Anyone but him!

00:23:59.890 --> 00:24:01.720
Preview
I think I picked the wrong topic.

00:24:01.720 --> 00:24:02.290
Preview

00:24:02.290 --> 00:24:05.730
Preview
The next episode is
"July 30, Saeta"

00:24:05.730 --> 00:24:07.190
Preview
We'll be waiting at Hidamari Apartments.

00:24:07.190 --> 00:24:09.130
Preview
Be sure to tune in!

00:24:09.130 --> 00:24:09.990
Preview
